    dct:type "resolution-route/computation" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.82"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Large bounded spaces can be simulated now and give informative comparisons. No sampling scheme or dataset covers all simple programs, and conclusions depend on encoding and complexity definitions." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Construct matched rule ensembles in one, two, and three dimensions for specified formalisms, classify behavior with common complexity measures, and compare prevalence and attainable classes. Similar rates support dimension-independence within those ensembles; large systematic differences refute it there." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Rule ensembles across dimensions are not canonically comparable.", "Fundamentally change and significant complexity are vague.", "The scope spans several infinite formalism classes." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/wolfram2002-ch05-01--gpt--dataset-1> .
